# ProductOS is licensed to the member, not the public — its own material
# (templates, checklists, BONUS best-practice docs, skills, onboarding
# references) stays untracked. The founder's own filled-in work products are
# tracked, because losing that folder would otherwise lose the entire Define
# and Design phases.
productos/*
!productos/define/
!productos/design/
productos/define/*
productos/design/*

# Define-phase work products
!productos/define/1-Product-Offer.md
!productos/define/2-Customer-Persona.md
!productos/define/2b-Persona-Set.md
!productos/define/3-Pricing-Strategy.md

# Design-phase work products
!productos/design/1-Product-Identity.md
!productos/design/2-Magic-Moment.md
!productos/design/3-Onboarding-Flow.md
!productos/design/4a-Landing-Page.md
!productos/design/Design-Prompts.md
!productos/design/V0-PROMPT-shortlist.md
!productos/design/onboarding-wireframe.html
!productos/design/landing-page-wireframe.html

# Local-only private notes — never tracked, at any path.
# Competitor research lives here on purpose: it is useful to us and it is not
# ours to publish. docs/COMPETITOR-ANALYSIS.local.md and docs/PARITY.local.md
# name specific companies and stay out of the repository.
*.local.md

node_modules/
# All env variants, not just the two we happen to use today.
.env
.env*
.DS_Store
.next/
.vercel/

# --- Next.js / toolchain ---
/.next/
/out/
/build
/coverage
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
.pnp
.pnp.*
*.pem
npm-debug.log*
.vercel

# The harvested candidate list — 4 MB+ of Common Crawl output, rewritten whole
# on every harvest and every qualification run. Regenerate with
# `npm run registry:harvest`; it touches no employer's server.
#
# ⚠️ IT CARRIES THE PROBE RESULTS TOO (probedAt, india, roles). Deleting it does
# not lose the registry — registry/boards.json is the curated file and IS
# tracked — but it does throw away tens of thousands of live ATS probes, so the
# next qualification run redoes all of them. Keep the file; just don't version it.
registry/candidates.json

# Competitor material — never tracked, at any path.
#
# Research that names other firms is useful to us and is not ours to publish.
# It lives in *.local.md (already ignored above) and in the patterns below.
# ⚠️ THIS ONLY STOPS FUTURE COMMITS. Names already written into commit MESSAGES
# are in the history and an ignore rule cannot reach them — see the note in
# docs/CONFLICTS.md about what removing them would cost.
# Patterns are deliberately generic and name no firm — a rule that spells a
# company out is itself the thing being avoided, in a tracked file.
*COMPETITOR*
*competitor*
*ANALYSIS*
*analysis*
*PARITY*
*parity*
